Reference data were pulled from Wei et al. (2024), Nature NUMT paper.

1) Download Reference NUMTs:
  a) Reference Numts data comes from: https://github.com/mills-lab/dinumt/blob/master/refNumts.38.bed 
    wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mills-lab/dinumt/master/refNumts.38.bed 

2) Download Non-reference Germline NUMTs: 
    https://github.com/mills-lab/numts-and-aging-in-fibroblasts-and-brains/tree/main/callset/Numt
  a) wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mills-lab/numts-and-aging-in-fibroblasts-and-brains/main/callset/Numt/Numt.1000G.20221202.tar.gz
  b) tar -xzvf Numt.1000G.20221202.tar.gz
  - Using: Numt.1000G/ALL.dinumt.NumtS.1000G.HC.20200604.gt.vcf.gz * Numt.1000G/ directory
    bcftools query -f '%CHROM\t%POS0\t%END\n' ALL.dinumt.NumtS.1000G.HC.20200604.gt.vcf.gz > GermLineNumt1000g.bed

3) Filter Your Data:
    # Convert the numts calls txt file Palmer outputs to a bed format
    awk 'NR>1 {print $2"\t"$3"\t"$5"\t"$1"\t"$12"\t"$15}' Output_numts_calls.txt > all_numts.bed

    # Add 25 bp upstream and downstream
    bedtools slop -i all_numts.bed -g hg38.genome -b 25 > all_numts.slop25.bed
    bedtools slop -i refNumts.38.bed -g hg38.genome -b 25 > refNumts.slop25.bed
    bedtools slop -i GermLineNumt1000g.bed -g hg38.genome -b 25 > germline.slop25.bed
    
    # Merge reference and germline NUMTs separately
    sort -k1,1 -k2,2n refNumts.slop25.bed | bedtools merge > refNumts.merged.bed
    sort -k1,1 -k2,2n germline.slop25.bed | bedtools merge > germline.merged.bed
    sort -k1,1 -k2,2n all_numts.slop25.bed | bedtools merge > all_numts.merged.bed
  
    # Merge PALMER calls (with buffer) to handle nearby calls
    bedtools intersect -v -a all_numts.merged.bed -b germline.merged.bed > overlapping_germline.bed
    bedtools intersect -v -a all_numts.merged.bed -b refNumts.merged.bed > overlapping_reference.bed
 
    # Combine reference + germline and merge again
    cat refNumts.merged.bed germline.merged.bed | sort -k1,1 -k2,2n | bedtools merge > exclude_all.bed
    bedtools intersect -v -a all_numts.merged.bed -b exclude_all.bed > somatic_candidates.bed


    
    # Get full PALMER info for germline, reference, and somatic calls
    bedtools intersect -wa -wb -a overlapping_germline.bed -b all_numts.bed > overlapping_germline_full.txt
    bedtools intersect -wa -wb -a overlapping_reference.bed -b all_numts.bed > overlapping_reference_full.txt
    bedtools intersect -wa -wb -a somatic_candidates.bed -b all_numts.bed > somatic_candidates_full.txt

